    - trzy_noce == rozkopany_grob:
        The priest received him in the sacristy without offering his hand. He listened, and then said that he would help—but first Jaromir must beg forgiveness before the whole parish for desecrating old Wójcik’s grave. That very day, at vespers on the feast of St John, he knelt before the altar on the bare stone floor, while the people of Bukowiec whispered behind his back.
    - pochowek_wojcika == pochowany_za_murem:
        The priest received him in the sacristy without offering his hand. He would help—but first Jaromir must confess before the whole parish that he had buried a Christian like a heathen, outside the wall. That very day, at vespers on the feast of St John, he knelt before the altar on the bare stone floor, while the people of Bukowiec whispered behind his back.
    - pochowek_wojcika == pochowany_z_makiem:
        The priest received him coldly. He would help—if Hanka, whom he had turned away from communion a year and a half before, after old Wójcik’s funeral, confessed to the poppy seed before the whole parish. Hanka went that very day, to vespers on the feast of St John. She knelt before the altar through the whole service and never once raised her head.
    - else:
        The priest received him at once, in the presbytery kitchen, over a bowl of soup that Jaromir did not touch.
    }
    “The child was lost on the night of the heathen fires,” said the priest. “Small wonder.” He sighed. “But God does not abandon His own.”
    ~ ekwipunek += rozaniec
    He blessed a rosary and a flask of water for Jaromir, and then for a long while said nothing. # pokaz: woda
    “My predecessor wrote strange things in the parish books,” he said at last, more quietly. “That once in a few score years a child vanishes from a village under the forest. Always on the same night. And that those who come back remember nothing.” He laid a hand on Jaromir’s shoulder. “Swear to me on this rosary that you will have done with heathen ways. With herbs at the windows, with fires, with gifts for whatever lives in the water. Then I shall pray for you every day until you return.”
    Jaromir swore. # tobolek # dalej
*   [Send Józek for the planetnik.]
    ~ rada_przed_borem = rada_planetnika
    ~ pole_zbite_gradem = true
    # tlo: planetnik_burza
    “There’s one such,” said Staś. “He walks ahead of the storms. Whoever gives him bread, the clouds won’t burst over his field. He knows where everything is, for he looks down on it all from above. Let Józek run up to Beech Ridge. You can always see him there when he’s passing.”
    ~ zapiski += planetnik_1
    The planetnik came towards evening, as black clouds were rolling in from the west—a tall old man in rags, his beard tossed by the wind, a sack on his back and a rope in his hand whose other end vanished somewhere high above, in the billows over his head. He smelled of rain and wet stone, like the air just before a thunderbolt. # pokaz: planetnik
    He ate the bread Hanka gave him, and then looked at Jaromir with eyes as cold and bright as hailstones.
    “Over the forest the clouds part,” he said. “Not a drop has fallen there for as long as people can remember. Where it doesn’t rain, that’s where to look for her.”
    He jerked the rope, and the clouds above him moved off. As he was leaving, he called back over his shoulder:
    “And you’ll pay for the knowing, like everyone. Your field I’ll take.”
    Before midnight a hailstorm passed over Zapadlina, the stones as big as pigeons’ eggs. It beat down everything growing on Jaromir’s strips—and not a single ear at the neighbours’. # pokaz: grad # dalej
